WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.435
An aircraft gearbox develops increasing
vibration during steady cruise. The symptom

00:00:04.435 --> 00:00:08.874
persists in a ground check. The investigation
must distinguish a mechanical source from

00:00:08.874 --> 00:00:11.680
sensor installation using flight and ground
recordings.

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:17.180
I give MachinePulseAI Agent the problem and
recordings, asking it to compare possible

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:19.040
causes and report the evidence.

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:25.707
Local Qwen3 Coder 30B opens the recordings,
checks channel quality and configures and runs

00:00:25.707 --> 00:00:27.030
the analysis tools.

00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:35.573
The Agent first compares speed, torque and
vibration in early and late flight windows.

00:00:35.573 --> 00:00:43.622
Spectra and measured-encoder analysis help
assess the components alongside rotational

00:00:43.622 --> 00:00:44.190
speed.

00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:51.599
RAG retrieves the applicable sensor roles and
bearing geometry. The geometry guides the

00:00:51.599 --> 00:00:58.365
expected-frequency comparison. Indexed
documents persist in the local Knowledge Base

00:00:58.365 --> 00:01:03.360
and can be retrieved for relevant questions in
later sessions.

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:09.680
The approximately 107.4 Hz outer-race family
is supported by both sensors in both

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:16.184
recordings, with five harmonic matches in all
four analyses. Persistence after remounting

00:01:16.184 --> 00:01:20.130
weakens a single-sensor installation-only
explanation.

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:26.933
The evidence focuses the next physical
inspection on the bearing. An engineer reviews

00:01:26.933 --> 00:01:32.657
the report interpretation, including
corrections in this run. The assessment

00:01:32.657 --> 00:01:39.060
presents the measured signature, alternatives
and physical confirmation still needed.

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:45.692
The latest report brings the assessment,
computed plots, measurements and citations

00:01:45.692 --> 00:01:52.524
together. The engineer can review the evidence
and choose the next test. Open this same PDF

00:01:52.524 --> 00:01:57.780
beside the video, or request a demonstration
with your test recording.
